{"id":"620760b4-784d-41b7-aac2-20967b024913","object":"chat.completion","created":1795095548,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT c.customer_unique_id AS customer_unique_id, COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS order_count\nFROM orders o\nJOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nWHERE c.customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL\nGROUP BY c.customer_unique_id\nORDER BY order_count DESC, c.customer_unique_id ASC\nLIMIT 10;","reasoning_content":"Need SQL: count orders per natural person (customer_unique_id) via orders join customers. Count distinct order_id. Top 10, order by count desc, unique_id asc.\n\nNeed output natural person ID and order count. Only known identity? \"按自然人统计订单数\" - 按人分组，不把NULL合并；默认只统计已知身份. So WHERE customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL. Is that adding filter? Entity policy says 人数和按人分组时不把SQL NULL身份合并成一个人；默认只统计已知身份. So filter null ok.\n\nSQL:\n\nSELECT c.customer_unique_id AS customer_unique_id, COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS order_count\nFROM orders o\nJOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nWHERE c.customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL\nGROUP BY c.customer_unique_id\nORDER BY order_count DESC, c.customer_unique_id ASC\nLIMIT 10;\n\nNote limit with ties? User says top 10 people, same count by ID asc -> LIMIT fine since deterministic. Top 10 rows.\n\nCould count o.order_id distinct; orders primary key so count(distinct o.order_id) fine. No need order_status filter.\n\nOutput no explanation."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3552,"completion_tokens":334,"total_tokens":3886,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":255},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1760},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}